# Musicplayer

Musicplayer is a GTK3 desktop music player with playlist, shuffle, playback
statistics, album-art, YouTube download, and spectrum-visualizer plugins.

## Build and install

```sh
aclocal
libtoolize
automake --add-missing
autoconf
./configure --disable-run-in-source-tree
make
sudo make install
```

`--disable-run-in-source-tree` makes the player load plugins from the
installation directory (`/usr/local/lib/musicplayer` by default). Run
`src/musicplayer` after rebuilding, or install again when testing installed
plugins.

## Playback UI

- Long track titles use a Cairo/Pango scroller; click the title to pause or
  resume scrolling.
- The playlist expands to fill the available window and collapses to its
  compact content size while remaining resizable.
- The visualizer can be configured for scale, placement, colors, bars, and
  line display.
- Playback statistics are shown in the status row and in a detailed dialog.

## Tests

Run the full test suite with:

```sh
make -C tests check
```
